       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose there's a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Overdoses can also cause non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema, and the effects can last a long time because the drug's half-life is 30 to 50 hours.\n\nPlease check which of these you meant:\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO daily.** This is the usual starting dose. A lower dose of 2.5 mg is sometimes used in frail or elderly patients.\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO daily.** This is the maximum standard dose.\n- **A different drug or dose.** Another medication may have been intended, or the 50 mg may be a typo.\n\nIf 50 mg is truly what you want, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
